(BAS-38 - the sentence-ownership worked example, LANGUAGE.md:125-132. The
 snippet in the manual is a FRAGMENT: `content`, `number_lines`, `output`
 and `source` are never declared and there is no `open`, so it cannot be
 compiled as printed. This is the faithful runnable form of it - same
 shape, same claim: the period after the inner `if` closes only that `if`,
 and the `while` body continues with the two actions after it.
 Reads docs/ledger/probes/basics/fixtures/lines.txt; run from the repo root.
