)
a boolean called 'number lines' is true.
a number called numbered is 0.
open a file for reading called source at "docs/ledger/probes/basics/fixtures/lines.txt".
a buffer called content is 64 bytes in size.
Read line from source into content.
While content is not empty,
    if 'number lines' then,
        print "{numbered}: " without newline.
    print content without newline,
    increment numbered,
    Read line from source into content.
Close source.
Print "read {numbered} lines".
